On 4/4/08, LakMeer Kravid <lakmeerkravid@gmail.com> wrote:
> coi rodo
>
> I have a few questions:
> 1) how does one assert "No/zero [somethings] exist"? Do I need to make
> a claim with {na zasti} or similar, or is there a way using numerals
> that's a bit more lobykai?

You can use {no}:

   no crida cu zasti lo traji raclypre
   "No fairies exist for the extreme rationalist."

> 2) I have a draft proposal for an original orthography, complete with
> truetype font. Where would be a good place to host it online for
> review and criticism?

Probably the wiki.

> 3) How badly would it screw with my grammar if I were to use a
> one-syllable rafsi in the place of a gismu, for rhythmic purposes in
> songwriting?

Very badly.

> It probably ceases to be parsable, but is it forgivable
> under the banner of 'artistic license'?

There are good chances it parses as something else.

